==Strategy==
This stage is rather tricky to clear, as the combination of Lord Gravey and Henry means that on difficulties up to 3 crowns, [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] is nearly indispensable (unless the player has appropriate Ubers), as she has enough range to stay within Henry's blindspot while also remaining out of reach from Gravey's attacks. [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] can one shot the Zuches, meaning that if you have this unit, then it is highly recommended to bring it as it will make the stage a lot easier.

Play this stage sort of like [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]], luring Henry and Gravey close to the base so you can time Cadaver BearCats to "snipe" unburrowing Zuches. You can bring [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] as a panic button to get a Zuche off your base fast if BearCat gets frozen. [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] can work too, but be wary that he usually cannot one-shot Zuche on 3-crown difficulty. 

Bring at least 2 meatshields: [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]] is great here as not only does it have freeze immunity, but it can effectively hold the line on its own once all the Zuches are dead. Additionally, it gains the ability to dodge zombies through talents, making it a great counter for this stage, especially in 4 crown difficulty. Another good meatshield to bring is [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]], as they can be useful at the initial Zuche waves, although too slow to reliably traverse Henry's wide range without being frozen.

You can use rushers such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Yukimura]] with a well-timed Thunderbolt Cat Cannon to deal high amounts of damage at time, though it is  unreliable due to the possibility of Lord Gravey killing them as soon as they reach him, resulting in a massive loss of cash.

The point of the stage is mainly to kill all the Zuche waves, then chip off Lord Gravey slowly but surely. Once Gravey is dead, you've essentially won the stage as Henry has no pushing power on his own and can easily be rushed down.

As with any zombie stage, a high level Holy Blast will help immensely. However, you actually do NOT want to unburrow Zuche. He outranges Cadaver BearCat and will usually hit the poor bear wannabe first, thus you should wait for its unburrow animation to snipe it with Cadaver. Use Holy Blast to chunk Gravey instead.

